{
  "slug": "paper-authoring-excellence",
  "description": "The canonical premium-paper guide for agents: the bulldocs publish door, the payload shape, the authoring laws, the top-10 block vocabulary with evidence devices, and every publish-wall error decoded — seeded from the Eight-Minute Erasure port's friction log.",
  "tags": [
    {
      "tag": "authoring-excellence",
      "strength": 90,
      "rationale": "the canonical agent onramp for authoring premium papers through the deck"
    },
    {
      "tag": "bulldocs",
      "strength": 70,
      "rationale": "documents the bulldocs publish door, payload contract and wall behavior"
    },
    {
      "tag": "bp-cli",
      "strength": 45,
      "rationale": "teaches the bp bulldocs and bp media upload command surface"
    }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "pax-eyebrow",
      "type": "eyebrow",
      "text": "BARKPARK · AGENT ONRAMP · CANONICAL PREMIUM-PAPER GUIDE"
    },
    {
      "id": "pax-h1",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "text": "Paper Authoring Excellence"
    },
    {
      "id": "pax-ingress",
      "type": "ingress",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "How an agent publishes a premium Paper through the real door — the payload shape, the authoring laws, the block vocabulary, and every wall error decoded. Seeded from the friction log of porting the Eight-Minute Erasure benchmark artifact into a native Paper. If you are about to hand-roll an HTML page: stop — the deck below expressed a 55 KB editorial evidence artifact with zero raw HTML."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "pax-h2-door",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "The door"
    },
    {
      "id": "pax-p-door1",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Papers are published by upserting a portable-doc payload to a slug. The CLI door:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "pax-code-door",
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "bash",
      "value": "bp bulldocs publish <slug> --file payload.json --yes\n# HTTP (ingest token):\n#   POST /v1/plugins/bulldocs/papers        (canonical)\n#   POST /v1/paperflow/papers               (back-compat alias)\n# The paper renders live at /papers/<slug>."
    },
    {
      "id": "pax-p-door2",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "The slug must ALSO be a top-level key inside the JSON — the CLI does not inject the positional argument. Publishing the same slug again upserts in place. "
        },
        {
          "type": "strong",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "Do not use the body_html path"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": ": it is a degradation, not a door — an HTML-only paper collapses to run-together text in the terminal reader and is invisible to every block-aware surface (editor, email, TUI, patch ops)."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "pax-h2-shape",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "The payload shape"
    },
    {
      "id": "pax-code-shape",
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "json",
      "value": "{\n  \"slug\": \"my-paper\",\n  \"description\": \"At least 20 characters describing the paper.\",\n  \"tags\": [\n    {\"tag\": \"authoring-excellence\", \"strength\": 90,\n     \"rationale\": \"at least 20 characters on why this tag\"},\n    {\"tag\": \"bulldocs\", \"strength\": 60,\n     \"rationale\": \"registered tags only; distinct strengths\"}\n  ],\n  \"blocks\": [\n    {\"id\": \"b1\", \"type\": \"eyebrow\", \"text\": \"KICKER · CONTEXT LINE\"},\n    {\"id\": \"b2\", \"type\": \"heading\", \"level\": 1, \"text\": \"The title\"},\n    {\"id\": \"b3\", \"type\": \"ingress\",\n     \"content\": [{\"type\": \"text\", \"value\": \"The standfirst paragraph.\"}]},\n    {\"id\": \"b4\", \"type\": \"paragraph\",\n     \"content\": [{\"type\": \"text\", \"value\": \"Body prose. Inline leaves are \"},\n                 {\"type\": \"strong\", \"children\": [{\"type\": \"text\", \"value\": \"value-keyed\"}]},\n                 {\"type\": \"text\", \"value\": \", always.\"}]}\n  ]\n}"
    },
    {
      "id": "pax-p-shape1",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "The paper's title is the level-1 "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "value": "heading"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": " block (content-first doctrine: title and featured image are body blocks, not metadata). Every "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "value": "tags[].tag"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": " must be a registered tag document — "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "value": "bp doc ls tag"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": " lists them — with 2–4 weighted entries, distinct strengths (the max marks the main tag), and rationales of at least 20 characters. The description must also clear 20 characters."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "pax-h2-laws",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "The authoring laws"
    },
    {
      "id": "pax-p-laws0",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Each law below was proven live — violate it and the wall refuses, or worse, the reader silently drops your content behind a 200."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "pax-laws",
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": true,
      "items": [
        [
          {
            "type": "strong",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "value": "Inline leaves are value-keyed."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": " Every text leaf is "
          },
          {
            "type": "code",
            "value": "{\"type\":\"text\",\"value\":\"…\"}"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": ". A "
          },
          {
            "type": "code",
            "value": "text"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "-keyed leaf renders as the EMPTY string — the paragraph publishes fine and then vanishes on the page. This is the worst failure class: no error, no placeholder, just missing prose."
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "type": "strong",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "value": "Table cells are maps or content arrays."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": " A cell is either "
          },
          {
            "type": "code",
            "value": "{\"text\":\"…\"}"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": " or an inline-content array "
          },
          {
            "type": "code",
            "value": "[{\"type\":\"text\",\"value\":\"…\"}]"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": ". Bare strings are refused: “paper contains block content that readers cannot render … has no renderable inline content”."
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "type": "strong",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "value": "Grid span and order are top-level child keys."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": " On a "
          },
          {
            "type": "code",
            "value": "section"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": " grid child, write "
          },
          {
            "type": "code",
            "value": "\"span\": 2"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": " beside "
          },
          {
            "type": "code",
            "value": "\"type\""
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": ", never inside a "
          },
          {
            "type": "code",
            "value": "layout"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": " map — nested placement is ignored."
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "type": "strong",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "value": "Code blocks carry source under the value key."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": " "
          },
          {
            "type": "code",
            "value": "{\"type\":\"code\",\"lang\":\"elixir\",\"value\":\"…\"}"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": ". A "
          },
          {
            "type": "code",
            "value": "code"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "-keyed source renders an empty "
          },
          {
            "type": "code",
            "value": "<pre>"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "."
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "type": "strong",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "value": "Zero empty-paragraph spacers."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": " Spacing is reader-owned — the shared reader tokens own section rhythm, and empty paragraphs are editor scaffolds the doctrine forbids in published payloads (351 were purged from the corpus)."
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "type": "strong",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "value": "container is not a block type."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": " It renders an Unsupported placeholder and silently DROPS its children. Nest with "
          },
          {
            "type": "code",
            "value": "section"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": " (optionally "
          },
          {
            "type": "code",
            "value": "\"layout\":{\"mode\":\"grid\",\"tracks\":2}"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "), "
          },
          {
            "type": "code",
            "value": "columns"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": ", or "
          },
          {
            "type": "code",
            "value": "figure"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "."
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "type": "strong",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "value": "Asciicast sources must be hosted URLs."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": " "
          },
          {
            "type": "code",
            "value": "data:"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": " URIs are silently neutered to "
          },
          {
            "type": "code",
            "value": "#"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": " at render. Upload the "
          },
          {
            "type": "code",
            "value": ".cast"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": " file via "
          },
          {
            "type": "code",
            "value": "bp media upload recording.cast --yes"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": " and use the returned "
          },
          {
            "type": "code",
            "value": "/media/files/…"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": " path."
          }
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "pax-h2-vocab",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "The top-10 block vocabulary"
    },
    {
      "id": "pax-p-vocab0",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "The renderer speaks ~56 types; these ten cover almost every paper (they are 96% of all published blocks). Shapes below are the load-bearing keys only — every block also takes an "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "value": "id"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "pax-vocab",
      "type": "table",
      "head": [
        [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Block"
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Shape essentials"
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Use for"
          }
        ]
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          [
            {
              "type": "code",
              "value": "paragraph"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "type": "code",
              "value": "content: [inline…]"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "body prose; inline marks: strong, em, code, link"
            }
          ]
        ],
        [
          [
            {
              "type": "code",
              "value": "heading"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "type": "code",
              "value": "level: 1–4, text: \"…\""
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "level 1 is the paper title; plain text only, no inline marks"
            }
          ]
        ],
        [
          [
            {
              "type": "code",
              "value": "ingress"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "type": "code",
              "value": "content: [inline…]"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "the standfirst under the title"
            }
          ]
        ],
        [
          [
            {
              "type": "code",
              "value": "eyebrow"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "type": "code",
              "value": "text: \"…\""
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "the kicker line above the title, or a section label"
            }
          ]
        ],
        [
          [
            {
              "type": "code",
              "value": "list"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "type": "code",
              "value": "ordered: bool, items: [[inline…]]"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "each item is an inline-content array"
            }
          ]
        ],
        [
          [
            {
              "type": "code",
              "value": "table"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "type": "code",
              "value": "head: [cell], rows: [[cell]]"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "cells are content arrays or text-keyed maps, never bare strings"
            }
          ]
        ],
        [
          [
            {
              "type": "code",
              "value": "callout"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "type": "code",
              "value": "title, tone: info|success|warning|danger|neutral, content"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "verdicts, warnings, quoted evidence rails"
            }
          ]
        ],
        [
          [
            {
              "type": "code",
              "value": "code"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "type": "code",
              "value": "lang, value: \"source\""
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "source, transcripts, command lines"
            }
          ]
        ],
        [
          [
            {
              "type": "code",
              "value": "stats"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "type": "code",
              "value": "items: [{label, value, spark?}]"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "stat tiles; spark takes a numeric array"
            }
          ]
        ],
        [
          [
            {
              "type": "code",
              "value": "section"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "type": "code",
              "value": "blocks: […], layout: {mode: \"grid\", tracks: N}"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "grouping and grid layout; children may carry top-level span"
            }
          ]
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "pax-h2-devices",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "The evidence devices"
    },
    {
      "id": "pax-p-dev0",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "A premium paper shows its receipts. Five deck devices carry evidence natively — all five are live on the worked example, "
        },
        {
          "type": "link",
          "href": "/papers/eight-minute-erasure",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "the Eight-Minute Erasure twin"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": ":"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "pax-devices",
      "type": "table",
      "head": [
        [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Device"
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Shape"
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "What it proves"
          }
        ]
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          [
            {
              "type": "code",
              "value": "asciicast"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "type": "code",
              "value": "src: \"/media/files/….cast\", caption"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "a replayable terminal session — the strongest “this actually ran” device; pair it with an expandable transcript"
            }
          ]
        ],
        [
          [
            {
              "type": "code",
              "value": "expandable"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "type": "code",
              "value": "summary: \"…\", children: [blocks]"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "full transcripts and long appendices without crushing the page; closed expandables are exempt from first-pass word caps"
            }
          ]
        ],
        [
          [
            {
              "type": "code",
              "value": "diagram"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "type": "code",
              "value": "source: \"mermaid…\", caption"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "mermaid hydrates natively on the reader AND draws in the TUI; double-quote every label"
            }
          ]
        ],
        [
          [
            {
              "type": "code",
              "value": "chart"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "type": "code",
              "value": "series + annotations: regions, refLines, points"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "measured data with verdict annotations — regions and reference lines nobody else uses yet"
            }
          ]
        ],
        [
          [
            {
              "type": "code",
              "value": "stats"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "type": "code",
              "value": "items: [{label, value, spark?}]"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "headline numbers with per-item sparklines"
            }
          ]
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "pax-h2-errors",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Wall errors decoded"
    },
    {
      "id": "pax-errors",
      "type": "table",
      "head": [
        [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "What you see"
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "What it means"
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "The fix"
          }
        ]
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "“paper contains block content that readers cannot render” + a blocks[] path list"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "a cell, list item, or nested block has no renderable inline shape (bare string cells are the classic)"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "rewrite the named paths as content arrays or text-keyed maps, republish"
            }
          ]
        ],
        [
          [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "“publish references unregistered tag(s)” + suggestions"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "a tags[].tag names no registered tag document"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "pick from details.suggestions, or register the tag as a type:tag doc, then republish"
            }
          ]
        ],
        [
          [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "409 duplicate / similarity refusal"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "the dedup wall matched your title/description/tags against an existing paper"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "differentiate the title and description, rebalance tag weights, republish"
            }
          ]
        ],
        [
          [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "422 with details.failures (block/heading/word caps)"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "the epic-quality caps — 80 blocks, 16 headings, 5,000 first-pass words — which bind ONLY papers tagged epic-cycle-wave-paper"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "trim, or move appendices into closed expandables (exempt); ordinary papers never hit these caps"
            }
          ]
        ],
        [
          [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "400 malformed"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "the payload lacks slug plus blocks (or body_html)"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "send slug top-level AND in the file; blocks must be a list"
            }
          ]
        ],
        [
          [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "warning[label_norm] on success"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "advisory band, not a refusal — tag count outside the 2–4 norm"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "tune tags; the paper is already live"
            }
          ]
        ],
        [
          [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "nothing at all — a 200, and content missing on the page"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "the silent classes: text-keyed leaves, container children, data: URIs, plain-string notes items"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "author to the laws above; curl the rendered page and grep for your sentences before calling it done"
            }
          ]
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "pax-p-verify",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "The last row is the discipline that matters most: "
        },
        {
          "type": "strong",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "a 200 is not a render."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": " After publishing, fetch "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "value": "/papers/<slug>"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": " and grep for a distinctive sentence from every section you authored. The twin's port did exactly that and shipped with zero silent drops."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "pax-callout-close",
      "type": "callout",
      "tone": "info",
      "title": "The worked example",
      "content": [
